可以按这个逻辑写，不要偏离。

### Paragraph 1：问题

GUI agents are commonly trained and evaluated through coordinate/action generation. This formulation is convenient, but it conflates two computations: identifying the target region and serializing that region into a coordinate protocol.

### Paragraph 2：观察

We find that these two computations are not aligned in depth. Intermediate layers often decode the target region better than final layers, even though final layers are closer to the output tokens.

### Paragraph 3：假说

We call this discrepancy the coordinate serialization bottleneck. The model first forms a spatial intent in screen space; later layers transform this intent into vocabulary-level action coordinates.

### Paragraph 4：证据

Across GUI-Owl, UI-TARS, and UI-Venus variants, best single layers consistently appear before final layers. On SS-Pro, Qwen2.5-VL agents peak around L20–L21 and degrade sharply afterwards; Qwen3-VL agents peak around L22–L26 with a wider plateau.

### Paragraph 5：方法

Based on this observation, we introduce ZwerGe-UI, a layerwise spatial posterior framework that reads intermediate representations and uses them for grounding and optional local refinement.

